namespace Submission

/-- **Existence of a non-isotopic pair of oriented smooth knots.**

We take `K₁` to be the unknot (round unit circle in the `xy`-plane) and `K₂` the smooth cusp knot
`Submission.CuspKnotMap.cuspKnot` (the algebraic `(2,3)`-torus / cusp link realized in `ℝ³` by
stereographic projection from the weighted sphere).  By
`Submission.Helpers.isotopic_imp_ambient_homeo`, any ambient isotopy carrying one to the other
would induce a homeomorphism of `ℝ³` taking the image of the unknot onto the image of the cusp
knot; `Submission.Helpers.no_ambient_homeo_unknot_cuspKnot` rules this out (the unknot complement
has abelian `π₁`, the cusp-knot complement does not). -/
theorem exists_nonisotopic_knots : ∃ K₁ K₂ : Knot, ¬ K₁.Isotopic K₂ :=
  ⟨Helpers.unknot, Submission.CuspKnotMap.cuspKnot, fun h =>
    Helpers.no_ambient_homeo_unknot_cuspKnot (Helpers.isotopic_imp_ambient_homeo _ _ h)⟩

end Submission
